        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="urCOEpVtA5ZqRUnClqoD-4" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 30px;&quot;&gt;Dealing with the Pug from the other side of the &#39;blockade&#39;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 30px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1200" y="2960" width="470" height="370" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fKeABDD7194liUzH6BVF-5" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;" parent="1" source="urCOEpVtA5ZqRUnClqoD-6" target="3jsujLA_XthRwtl_teJ9-1" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="urCOEpVtA5ZqRUnClqoD-6" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;The Wolfpack gets nukes from a pirate on Greenrock by paying him in uranium. I think the SYN and perhaps even FL should be part of supplying this warlord (at least initially). Maybe this is actually a decision point. Support the Wolfpack through an intermediary OR keep the nukes in house.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1580" y="1830" width="410" height="340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7sfs1GYAZ9bGBkHBiIdA-3" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" source="7sfs1GYAZ9bGBkHBiIdA-1" target="Dn4OLnnZR1lDdLMxqPTp-6" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7sfs1GYAZ9bGBkHBiIdA-1" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;Introduce the &quot;Class-C Freighter&quot; (aka secret drone carrier)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="1830" width="380" height="110" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="fKeABDD7194liUzH6BVF-4" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" source="7sfs1GYAZ9bGBkHBiIdA-5" target="urCOEpVtA5ZqRUnClqoD-6" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="7sfs1GYAZ9bGBkHBiIdA-5" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;Supply drop to Tundra: bring 10 tons of deuterium refining equipment to Tundra so the FW can use it to convert Smuggler&#39;s Den into a working refinery.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1060" y="1870" width="440" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="YjBwMqUuVJoWHoVx7JI9-2" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" source="YjBwMqUuVJoWHoVx7JI9-1" target="7sfs1GYAZ9bGBkHBiIdA-1" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="YjBwMqUuVJoWHoVx7JI9-1" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;A local pirate warlord is proving too troublesome. Eliminate them and their fleet so business can continue.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="50" y="1290" width="360" height="200" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="YjBwMqUuVJoWHoVx7JI9-3" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 30px;&quot;&gt;FL becomes part of the council and gets to make some decisions BEFORE checkmate/reconciliation. What sort of decisions can FL make in the SYN campaign? &lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3930" y="670" width="750" height="230" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="YjBwMqUuVJoWHoVx7JI9-4" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 30px;&quot;&gt;Should be some missions that let FL help with secretive SYN employees that then lead to helping the extremist faction.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3930" y="440" width="750" height="230" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="YjBwMqUuVJoWHoVx7JI9-6" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 36px;&quot;&gt;SYN promotion (FW FL joins The Council): 6k&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="950" y="2660" width="550" height="210" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="YjBwMqUuVJoWHoVx7JI9-27" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;entryX=0.5;entryY=0;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" parent="1" source="Dn4OLnnZR1lDdLMxqPTp-19" target="urCOEpVtA5ZqRUnClqoD-2" edge="1">
          <mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3jsujLA_XthRwtl_teJ9-1" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 30px;&quot;&gt;Without the Wolfpack and without the Defector, FW loses to the Republic. They control fewer planets and lose some others to piracy. The Navy does patrol more in the south, but not enough to get rid of all the pirate systems.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1510" y="2280" width="510" height="320" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3jsujLA_XthRwtl_teJ9-2" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;&quot;As thanks for your help against the Syndicate and the Pug, you&#39;ve been awarded a commendation and a small salary as a reward.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 24px;&quot;&gt;Salary: 2k&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="110" y="3840" width="430" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="3jsujLA_XthRwtl_teJ9-4" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 30px;&quot;&gt;Is the reason for the &#39;you have failed an essential FW mission&#39; alerts because there is no alternative campaign? Should there be a way to fail through a campaign? Is something like that only necessary (if it is necessary) for a 1.0 release as part of tying all the campaigns together?&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="3930" y="210" width="750" height="230" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="lITbNWXE8uC33C-zj884-1" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=1;jettySize=auto;html=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=1;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;" parent="1" source="Dn4OLnnZR1lDdLMxqPTp-9" target="Dn4OLnnZR1lDdLMxqPTp-9" edge="1">
